[city_factor_probe] WHY, and what it means for §14.1:
  The probe varied N (cells holding a derived-shaped row) while
  holding the map at 2048 cells. `refresh_city_modifier_factors`
  always does two O(map) passes first:
    (a) shared_factor x 156  -- GLOBAL + ENTITY(0) probes
    (b) paint_shared x 2048 cells = 317440 int32 writes
  when `shared_changed` (economy_runtime.cpp:7048-7061, because
  clear_epoch_metrics resets _city_factor_shared_* every epoch).
  Only AFTER those does collect_scope_ids decide the N cells, and
  the per-covered-cell loop (7085-7095) runs.

  => On a 2048-cell map the fixed term is ~4 x the variable term
     even at N=512. The plan's `covered_cells x 156` is the right
     model for LARGE countries (N approaching CELLS) but it is NOT
     the whole cost: the full-matrix repaint is charged on every
     epoch regardless of coverage.
  => M1 must therefore not budget the derived layer as
     `covered_cells x 156` alone. It has to either (i) publish the
     shared row once instead of repainting it, or (ii) count 156*N
     against the MAP, not against coverage.

